      "issue": "The claim that a blank attachment field suggests no approved temporary instruction attached before acceptance is an inference about process compliance rather than a direct fact. Evidence confirms the field was blank (finding-1yf38nl), but does not establish whether an approved instruction existed or what procedure governed its absence at issue time.",
      "evidenceNeeded": "Record of work-stage requirements for temporary instructions and evidence that such approval is required before acceptance signature; interview or log entry confirming crew intent to attach one if available.",
      "question": "What requirement governs whether a blank attachment field indicates non-compliance versus an acceptable state at issue time?"
    },
    "node-18bxeek": {
      "supported": false,
      "issue": "The claim that the field execution record was blank implies no recorded boundary verification or valve-state documentation is unsupported because a blank record does not prove absence of action. Evidence confirms WO-527-E was blank (finding-18a8qte), but does not establish whether any physical verification occurred.",
      "evidenceNeeded": "Interviews, logs, or photos showing if crew performed valve checks despite the missing form; evidence that a different record captured boundary state at issue time.",
      "question": "Did U-A/U-B perform and document any valve-state check before 10:00 AM even though WO-527-E was blank?"
    },
